// ESP32 GAME STATION
// FIXED-CLASS PSRAM BLOCK POOL CONTRACT
// 133_psram_pool.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Reserves a bounded set of contiguous backing regions.
// - Reuses fixed-size blocks without repeated heap allocation.
// - Selects the smallest available class that satisfies a request.
// - Tracks generation and lease identifiers to reject stale handles.
// - Reports reserved, requested, used and internally wasted bytes.
// - Allows all blocks to be released in constant bounded time.
//
// Memory rule:
// - Pool metadata stays in internal static storage inside the object.
// - Backing regions normally use MemoryPreference::PsramOnly.
// - DMA descriptors and DMA transfer buffers must not use this pool.
// - Frequently accessed tiny state should remain in internal RAM.
//
// Fragmentation rule:
// - MemoryManager is called only once for each enabled size class.
// - Individual acquire/release operations never call malloc or free.
// - A class stride is aligned once and reused for every block.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 134 implements this contract using MemoryManager.
// - Audio, PDF, emulator and game caches may share one configured pool.
// - ResourceBudgetCoordinator will validate the total reservation before
//   the pool is initialized.
